<tr class="high"><td>1</td><td>Very high</td><td>Prof. Joerg Vogel - RNA Biology of Bacterial Infections</td><td>Helmholtz Institute for RNA-based Infection Research / HZI</td><td>Wuerzburg</td><td>Bacterial ncRNA, RNA-seq, infection biology</td><td>Works on noncoding RNAs, RNA-binding proteins, bacterial pathogens, microbiome members, and infection-focused RNA deep sequencing.</td><td>Emphasize small RNA annotation, pathogen transcriptomics, Snakemake/HPC RNA-seq, and RNA regulation in infection.</td><td>https://www.helmholtz-hiri.de/en/research/organisation/teams/team/rna-biology-of-bacterial-infections/</td></tr>
<tr class="high"><td>2</td><td>Very high</td><td>Prof. Alexander Westermann - Host-Pathogen-Microbiota Interactions</td><td>Helmholtz Institute for RNA-based Infection Research / HZI</td><td>Wuerzburg</td><td>Host-pathogen-microbiota RNA biology</td><td>Focuses on ncRNAs in pathogens, host, and microbiota using RNA-seq-based technologies in complex infection settings.</td><td>Pitch dual host-pathogen RNA-seq, fungal/bacterial infection transcriptomics, and host immune-cell RNA analysis.</td><td>https://www.helmholtz-hzi.de/en/research/research-groups/details/host-pathogen-microbiota-interactions/</td></tr>
<tr class="high"><td>3</td><td>Very high</td><td>Jun.-Prof. Jens Hoer - Molecular Principles of RNA Phages</td><td>Helmholtz Institute for RNA-based Infection Research / HZI</td><td>Wuerzburg</td><td>RNA phages, microbial RNA, host takeover</td><td>Investigates RNA phage-host interactions, post-transcriptional regulation, and antibacterial strategies.</td><td>Highlight RNA biology, pathogen-focused transcriptomics, and ability to bridge wet lab with sequencing analysis.</td><td>https://www.helmholtz-hiri.de/en/research/organisation/teams/team/molecular-principles-of-rna-phages/</td></tr>
<tr class="high"><td>4</td><td>Very high</td><td>Jun.-Prof. Camilla Ciolli Mattioli - Systems Microbiology of Intracellular Pathogens</td><td>Helmholtz Institute for RNA-based Infection Research / HZI</td><td>Wuerzburg</td><td>Intracellular pathogens, systems microbiology, infection omics</td><td>Excellent match for microbial infection biology plus systems-level transcriptomics.</td><td>Emphasize host-pathogen RNA-seq, infection model thinking, and quantitative analysis.</td><td>https://www.helmholtz-hiri.de/en/research/</td></tr>
<tr class="high"><td>5</td><td>Very high</td><td>Prof. Antoine-Emmanuel Saliba - Single-cell Analysis</td><td>Helmholtz Institute for RNA-based Infection Research / HZI</td><td>Wuerzburg</td><td>Single-cell infection analysis, transcriptomics</td><td>Strong fit for host-pathogen gene-expression analysis and RNA-seq method development.</td><td>Position yourself as RNA-seq/small RNA scientist ready to extend into single-cell infection systems.</td><td>https://www.helmholtz-hiri.de/en/research/</td></tr>
<tr class="high"><td>6</td><td>Very high</td><td>Prof. Franziska Faber - RNA Biology of Gram-positive Bacteria</td><td>Helmholtz Institute for RNA-based Infection Research / HZI</td><td>Wuerzburg</td><td>Bacterial RNA biology, infection</td><td>Associated HIRI group centered on bacterial RNA regulation, close to your RNA/infection background.</td><td>Stress microbial RNA regulation and ability to build reproducible omics pipelines.</td><td>https://www.helmholtz-hiri.de/en/research/</td></tr>
<tr class="high"><td>7</td><td>Very high</td><td>Dr. Chase Beisel - RNA Synthetic Biology</td><td>Helmholtz Institute for RNA-based Infection Research / HZI</td><td>Wuerzburg</td><td>RNA engineering, microbial systems</td><td>RNA-centric microbial engineering and RNA-based tools connect well with pathogen RNA biology.</td><td>Pitch fungal/bacterial small RNA expertise and interest in programmable RNA approaches.</td><td>https://www.helmholtz-hiri.de/en/research/</td></tr>
<tr class="high"><td>8</td><td>Very high</td><td>Prof. Lars Barquist - Integrative Informatics for Infection Biology</td><td>Helmholtz Institute for RNA-based Infection Research / HZI</td><td>Wuerzburg</td><td>Infection bioinformatics, RNA-seq, microbial genomics</td><td>Strong computational infection biology group; likely values reproducible transcriptomics and microbial omics.</td><td>Use as a computational-leaning option; be honest you are wet-lab plus omics, not pure method developer.</td><td>https://www.helmholtz-hzi.de/en/research/research-groups/</td></tr>
<tr class="high"><td>9</td><td>Very high</td><td>Prof. Mathias Munschauer - Molecular Virology / RNA-protein Interactions</td><td>Heidelberg University / HIRI associated</td><td>Heidelberg</td><td>Viral RNA, lncRNA, infection biology</td><td>Studies RNA-protein interactions and RNA regulation in infection; excellent RNA biology overlap.</td><td>Highlight alternative splicing/RNA regulation, RNA-binding protein interest, and infection transcriptomics.</td><td>https://www.helmholtz-hiri.de/de/forschung/assoziierte-wissenschaftler-alumni/teams/team/lncrna-und-infektionsbiologie/</td></tr>
